# Implementation Plan — Modern Certificate Thumbnail Gallery for Career Profile

Transform the text-only "Verified Certifications" list on the Career Profile page into a modern, recruiter-friendly **Certificate Thumbnail Gallery** featuring visual certificate cards, thumbnail previews, skeleton loading states, card action menus, and an interactive fullscreen preview modal.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Backend File Streaming Endpoints:** We will add `GET /api/growth/documents/:id/file` and `GET /api/growth/documents/:id/thumbnail` to safely stream original certificate files and cached thumbnail previews directly from GridFS.
> - **No Pipeline Changes:** The certificate extraction engine and database schemas remain completely unchanged. This is purely a UI/UX & asset streaming layer.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend API Layer

#### [MODIFY] [growthProfile.types.ts](file:///c:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/backend/src/modules/growth/growthProfile.types.ts)
- Extend `CertificateDTO` to include `processingId`, `sourceDocumentId`, `fileUrl`, `thumbnailUrl`, `mimeType`, `fileName`, `credentialId`, and `rawConfidence`.

#### [MODIFY] [growthProfile.service.ts](file:///c:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/backend/src/modules/growth/growthProfile.service.ts)
- Populate `UaipUpload` details for each `CertificateRecord` when building `certificates` array in `getProfile`.
- Generate canonical `fileUrl` (`/api/growth/documents/:sourceDocumentId/file`) and `thumbnailUrl` (`/api/growth/documents/:sourceDocumentId/thumbnail`).

#### [MODIFY] [growth.controller.ts](file:///c:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/backend/src/modules/growth/growth.controller.ts) & [growthRoutes.ts](file:///c:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/backend/src/routes/growthRoutes.ts)
- Implement `streamDocumentFile` and `streamDocumentThumbnail` endpoints.
- Stream image/PDF buffers directly from GridFS with proper `Content-Type`, `Content-Disposition`, and `Cache-Control` headers.
- Use `sharp` to resize and compress image thumbnails (WebP/PNG, 500px width) with caching headers to avoid re-generating on every request.

